WEBVTT

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:17.142
You're...!

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:24.900
It's been about ten years, huh?

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.779
Good job keeping your
promise with me up to now.

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:35.953
I am Kodachi's supervisor
and a Shepherd, number 771.

00:00:35.953 --> 00:00:39.623
People call me Nanai.

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:41.750
You were a Shepherd, too?

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.252
That's right.

00:00:43.252 --> 00:00:47.714
And I'd like you to be one of us, too.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.342
A Shepherd? Me?

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:59.268
Now, shall we go? To the place
you have always yearned for--

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.545
The magic library, officially
known as the Library of Prayers.

00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:31.300
Welcome, Kyotaro Kakei.

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:45.189
<i>Writing down my aspirations</i>

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:47.941
<i>For the day when they will come true</i>

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:53.280
<i>The time has come when</i>
<i>I want to turn to the page I marked</i>

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.744
<i>Although there are things I lose</i>
<i>sight of with everything that happens</i>

00:01:58.744 --> 00:02:00.120
<i>Hey, it's all right</i>

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.041
<i>The start I'm embarking on is unexpected</i>

00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:06.877
<i>The memory that you couldn't erase</i>

00:02:06.877 --> 00:02:09.546
<i>Even that sad memory</i>

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:13.592
<i>I'll give it a different, happier reading</i>

00:02:13.592 --> 00:02:19.223
<i>I feel like just that will change everything</i>

00:02:19.223 --> 00:02:20.349
<i>All Right</i>

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:23.560
<i>So come now, the way you are!</i>

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.396
<i>Don't hide your weak self</i>

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:27.397
<i>On my Sheep </i>

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:31.068
<i>Let's meet riding on a dream</i>

00:02:31.068 --> 00:02:36.990
<i>Even just calling your name as</i>
<i>I write in this book of adventures</i>

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.826
<i>I'm not lost anymore</i>

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:43.539
<i>Let's start our journey together</i>

00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:51.296
<i>Yes... more of you and me!</i>

00:03:02.057 --> 00:03:06.228
"Episode 6: The Magic Library"

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.378
Can I have one?

00:03:31.378 --> 00:03:33.505
Sure! Be careful, they're hot.

00:03:33.505 --> 00:03:34.673
Thanks!

00:03:39.803 --> 00:03:41.972
Fresh baked are the best!

00:03:42.598 --> 00:03:45.225
Thanks for your help, Kana.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:49.688
I'm sure the library workers
will be happy with these, too!

00:03:51.481 --> 00:03:56.653
I don't think they'd approve of us if
we just give them cookies, though, huh?

00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:58.405
"Heartbeat" "Cherry Pie" "Paradise"

00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:07.164
The number you are dialing is not
in service. Please hang up and try--

00:04:07.748 --> 00:04:09.374
"Kyotaro Kakei"
"Call ended"

00:04:10.292 --> 00:04:12.669
Maybe he's in the shower?

00:04:21.512 --> 00:04:26.600
This library drifts in the
realm of people's unconscious.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.353
It exists in everyone's hearts.

00:04:29.353 --> 00:04:36.860
However, no one is conscious of it,
and only we Shepherds may enter.

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:41.698
Is it like a dream world...?

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:45.661
Kind of like a dream you can touch, maybe?

00:04:46.662 --> 00:04:52.918
In these books are written the pasts and
futures of all the people alive on this earth.

00:04:52.918 --> 00:04:57.339
We read them and
support people in their futures.

00:04:58.006 --> 00:05:02.511
No matter how hard we try,

00:05:02.511 --> 00:05:06.890
we end up focusing on the futures of those
with greater influence on mankind, though.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.603
"I want to live a better life..."

00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:14.773
"I want to be happy..."

00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:22.281
This library was born out
of those countless prayers.

00:05:30.289 --> 00:05:34.418
Too bad. Only Shepherds can read these.

00:05:35.377 --> 00:05:36.628
Can you read it?

00:05:36.628 --> 00:05:38.797
Of course.

00:05:38.797 --> 00:05:43.594
Woah, man this is crazy. Everyone has
these happy smiles on their faces...

00:05:43.594 --> 00:05:46.930
What a scene.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.015
Whose book is that?

00:05:48.015 --> 00:05:50.559
Hm, am I allowed to say?

00:05:51.977 --> 00:05:54.104
Your underwear's showing.

00:06:07.993 --> 00:06:09.995
Where did that brat go?

00:06:09.995 --> 00:06:11.496
Bring him back immediately!

00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:15.751
Jeez, we just picked on him a little.
He's so much trouble!

00:06:18.003 --> 00:06:20.255
It's no use...

00:06:20.255 --> 00:06:23.091
It has to exist somewhere...

00:06:23.091 --> 00:06:24.593
A book with all the answers...

00:06:24.593 --> 00:06:25.802
"Fairy Tales From Around the World"
A book with all the answers...

00:06:25.802 --> 00:06:30.224
A magic book that will
make me fearless after I read it!

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:32.893
It's not this book...

00:06:32.893 --> 00:06:37.105
Or this one, or this one, or this one!

00:06:44.071 --> 00:06:48.158
That library I always see in my dreams...

00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:50.911
Maybe there...

00:06:54.998 --> 00:06:56.959
Did you see something?

00:06:56.959 --> 00:06:59.711
Um, yes.

00:07:02.923 --> 00:07:07.469
I see, you're at the point where
if it's your own book, you can read it.

00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:09.429
Impressive.

00:07:13.267 --> 00:07:17.187
Your premonitions of the
future are the same thing.

00:07:17.187 --> 00:07:23.068
You have the power to fly to this
library with just your consciousness.

00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:27.698
You probably peeked inside the books
without knowing what they meant.

00:07:29.992 --> 00:07:32.286
You have a natural aptitude for it.

00:07:32.286 --> 00:07:37.165
If you truly desired it, you could
be a resident of this library.

00:07:37.165 --> 00:07:41.545
I just wanted to go to the magic library.

00:07:41.545 --> 00:07:44.923
It wasn't like I wanted to help anyone.

00:07:44.923 --> 00:07:47.217
Happy Project...

00:07:48.218 --> 00:07:54.433
You've started something interesting.
Have you had a change of heart?

00:07:54.433 --> 00:07:57.060
I just do odd jobs.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:02.274
We're like people who do odd jobs for mankind.

00:08:02.274 --> 00:08:07.196
We're those who serve mankind,
born out of people's desires.

00:08:07.196 --> 00:08:08.697
Leaving self behind,

00:08:08.697 --> 00:08:13.368
just wishing for people's happiness
and quietly presenting a path to them.

00:08:13.952 --> 00:08:19.124
Besides, you are already
doing the work of a Shepherd.

00:08:19.124 --> 00:08:20.667
What?

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:22.878
Tsugumi Shirasaki.

00:08:22.878 --> 00:08:27.466
You saved her using your ability
to see the future, remember?

00:08:35.224 --> 00:08:39.520
I'm sure you would be a good Shepherd.

00:08:40.812 --> 00:08:41.855
Kodachi.

00:08:41.855 --> 00:08:43.982
Yes?

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.986
Look after Kakei for a while.

00:08:47.986 --> 00:08:53.450
She is a Shepherd trainee,
so it's like she has a learner's permit.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.869
Yours is a learner's permit?

00:08:55.869 --> 00:08:57.412
What about it?

00:08:57.412 --> 00:09:01.834
Once you pass the second test,
you will also be a trainee.

00:09:01.834 --> 00:09:04.878
Then, you'll be able to
read all these books, too.

00:09:10.425 --> 00:09:13.720
Please give me some time.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.180
Of course.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.766
You should think about it carefully.

00:09:31.905 --> 00:09:33.198
My room?

00:09:33.198 --> 00:09:38.245
Shepherds use books as doors
and can teleport anywhere.

00:09:39.413 --> 00:09:42.249
Starting tomorrow,
you'll be shadowing me as I work.

00:09:42.249 --> 00:09:44.459
Just make sure you don't get in my way.

00:09:45.169 --> 00:09:47.379
Why me?

00:09:48.964 --> 00:09:52.885
One thing for sure is
that you can't play favorites.

00:09:52.885 --> 00:09:58.307
That means you have to treat everyone
the same--family, lovers, friends, strangers.

00:09:58.307 --> 00:10:01.727
If you choose someone, I guess it
means you throw the others away, huh?

00:10:01.727 --> 00:10:06.398
Yeah, who needs useless friends, anyway?

00:10:06.398 --> 00:10:09.109
Don't you have a natural
aptitude for that, too, Kakei?

00:10:09.109 --> 00:10:11.153
What do you mean?

00:10:11.153 --> 00:10:13.405
Ever since starting the Library Club,

00:10:13.405 --> 00:10:16.617
you haven't gotten especially
close to anyone, right?

00:10:17.826 --> 00:10:20.704
You don't have a girlfriend or a best friend...

00:10:20.704 --> 00:10:23.582
That level is just about right.

00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:39.097
Everything I desired was there.

00:10:39.097 --> 00:10:42.976
But becoming a Shepherd is something else.

00:10:42.976 --> 00:10:46.563
It's not like I want to make anyone happy...

00:10:46.563 --> 00:10:49.191
Even doing all that
with Shirasaki and the others

00:10:49.191 --> 00:10:52.903
is just me trying to understand my own feelings.

00:10:52.903 --> 00:10:57.783
What I want is be alone
in my own peaceful world.

00:10:57.783 --> 00:11:00.035
You've changed...

00:11:00.827 --> 00:11:02.746
Or...

00:11:05.958 --> 00:11:08.377
I need to apologize to you.

00:11:08.377 --> 00:11:09.670
Huh?

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:13.090
I read some of the
recent events in Kakei's life.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:18.720
In the end, the formation of the
Library Club had a very good influence on him.

00:11:20.222 --> 00:11:22.850
If you continue to work with him,

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:27.646
you will be closer to finding what
is most important for a Shepherd.

00:11:27.646 --> 00:11:29.231
Please work hard.

00:11:33.026 --> 00:11:36.321
Why did it turn out like that...?

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.622
If he would only start dating someone,

00:11:45.622 --> 00:11:49.084
then he wouldn't be a
Shepherd candidate anymore.

00:11:56.884 --> 00:11:59.845
Seriously... What an idiot...

00:12:07.394 --> 00:12:09.479
It's okay to cry...

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.488
Shocking.

00:12:25.078 --> 00:12:28.415
My little leopard gecko ran away!

00:12:28.415 --> 00:12:30.751
Please help me find him!

00:12:32.669 --> 00:12:35.422
Misono, you're okay with lizards and stuff?

00:12:35.422 --> 00:12:39.301
I actually kind of like them.
Their eyes are cute.

00:12:39.301 --> 00:12:41.720
But they eat bugs, huh?

00:12:42.054 --> 00:12:43.472
Misono, a bug!

00:12:43.472 --> 00:12:47.184
Huh? Come on, do you think I'd fall for that?

00:12:47.184 --> 00:12:49.186
No, I'm serious. Your shoulder.

00:12:54.191 --> 00:12:58.487
Get it off, get it off,
get it off! Please get it off!

00:12:58.487 --> 00:13:01.240
I-It's fine! It's gone already!

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:02.950
What are you doing?

00:13:05.994 --> 00:13:07.079
Miyu!

00:13:07.079 --> 00:13:08.622
You're...

00:13:10.374 --> 00:13:12.793
You're from the Broadcasting Club...

00:13:12.793 --> 00:13:14.795
So it's true...

00:13:14.795 --> 00:13:19.049
You don't practice, and you
just play around every day...

00:13:19.049 --> 00:13:19.967
Miyu--

00:13:19.967 --> 00:13:22.261
Serizawa, it has nothing to do with you.

00:13:22.261 --> 00:13:26.682
Then the rumor that you skipped out
on your special lesson is true, too?

00:13:27.474 --> 00:13:29.434
What if it is?

00:13:29.434 --> 00:13:33.647
I can't believe I was even
the tiniest bit your friend!

00:13:33.647 --> 00:13:38.610
If you don't intend to work, then you
should leave this school! You're an eyesore!

00:13:41.822 --> 00:13:43.073
Misono!

00:13:47.953 --> 00:13:49.246
Idiot...

00:13:52.499 --> 00:13:53.876
Misono!

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:58.547
Hey, do you want to go somewhere fun?

00:13:58.547 --> 00:14:00.424
Um... but...

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:04.219
You don't want to if it's with me?

00:14:07.306 --> 00:14:09.975
Sorry!

00:14:09.975 --> 00:14:14.229
Kakei and I have some things to do!

00:14:15.272 --> 00:14:18.609
What? Kakei is with Kodachi?

00:14:18.609 --> 00:14:23.155
Yes. The two of them left together in a hurry.

00:14:23.155 --> 00:14:30.621
Kakei promised last night that I could
have him all to myself today, babe.

00:14:30.621 --> 00:14:35.209
Oho, things between
those two are progressing fast.

00:14:35.209 --> 00:14:38.921
I-I-I'll bring the library workers some snacks!

00:14:38.921 --> 00:14:40.881
Wait! What are you bringing?

00:14:40.881 --> 00:14:42.799
Uh... Should I bring tea, too?

00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:45.010
There's no tea that would go with "gecko"!

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:47.638
--Giza, you're the only one
--What do you think about how she said "babe"?!

00:14:47.638 --> 00:14:49.264
--who understands how I feel.
--What do you think about how she said "babe"?!

00:14:49.264 --> 00:14:51.266
--Don't cry, baby.
--Um... do you want half?

00:14:52.392 --> 00:14:53.352
"Shiomi Academy"
"Student Cafeteria - Appllio"

00:14:53.352 --> 00:14:55.187
This is where you're working?

00:14:55.187 --> 00:14:56.897
Take this seriously, okay?

00:14:56.897 --> 00:15:00.234
The target is someone you've
been involved with before.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:03.862
Don't tell me it's Ureshino?

00:15:03.862 --> 00:15:05.239
Bingo.

00:15:13.664 --> 00:15:17.000
This is a diagram of Sayumi Ureshino's life.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.294
The part that's lit up is where we are now.

00:15:19.294 --> 00:15:22.297
This is Ureshino's life?

00:15:22.297 --> 00:15:24.883
She has the potential to
develop a software program

00:15:24.883 --> 00:15:28.262
that could completely
change the lives of mankind.

00:15:28.262 --> 00:15:32.891
But she is about to injure her left hand badly.

00:15:32.891 --> 00:15:37.312
If that happens, she would have
to abandon becoming a programmer

00:15:37.312 --> 00:15:41.400
and live a life that she
would not consider happy.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:45.654
In other words, our job is to keep
Ureshino from getting hurt, huh?

00:15:45.654 --> 00:15:46.989
That's right.

00:15:47.823 --> 00:15:50.325
--Welcome!
--Welcome!

00:15:51.451 --> 00:15:56.623
17th from the entrance, 6th from the window.

00:15:57.499 --> 00:15:58.876
Here, huh?

00:16:00.294 --> 00:16:01.420
Okay, all set.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.546
With this?

00:16:02.546 --> 00:16:04.631
You'll see. Just watch.

00:16:11.096 --> 00:16:15.851
Oh my, Yuka will be punished
with a stun grenade for this later.

00:16:16.435 --> 00:16:21.565
The little lamb, Yuka, will discover a new
kind of pleasure from this punishment.

00:16:21.565 --> 00:16:23.984
That's life changing in a lot of different ways.

00:16:30.282 --> 00:16:33.493
Did I miscount the number of seats?

00:16:36.038 --> 00:16:39.041
Wh-What do we do? We have to stop her--

00:16:39.041 --> 00:16:41.168
Ureshino!

00:16:41.835 --> 00:16:43.337
Yes?

00:16:44.546 --> 00:16:48.175
I'm gonna take a shot at your heart!

00:16:48.175 --> 00:16:49.593
"Shoot!!"
Swoon!

00:16:49.593 --> 00:16:50.844
"Swoon!!"

00:16:51.136 --> 00:16:52.513
"Swoon!!"

00:16:57.976 --> 00:16:58.477
"I"

00:16:58.477 --> 00:16:58.769
"am"

00:16:58.769 --> 00:16:59.686
"finished"

00:16:59.686 --> 00:17:00.479
"I am finished!!"

00:17:00.687 --> 00:17:03.190
Wow, he stopped time!

00:17:09.821 --> 00:17:11.031
I did it...

00:17:12.491 --> 00:17:14.993
Oh my! Oh my, oh my, oh my!

00:17:14.993 --> 00:17:18.247
Oh my, oh my, oh my, oh my!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.708
Oh, Kakei, you little--

00:17:21.708 --> 00:17:24.336
Saying such embarrassing things in public!

00:17:25.712 --> 00:17:28.799
You made my heart skip a little!

00:17:30.008 --> 00:17:34.179
Well, I'm glad Ureshino
didn't end up getting hurt.

00:17:34.179 --> 00:17:38.433
Sorry, you really saved me.

00:17:38.433 --> 00:17:41.353
If you hadn't been there, I would've failed.

00:17:42.229 --> 00:17:47.150
You should be more careful next time.
You're my senior, aren't you?

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:52.781
Uh, y-yeah... I will. Thanks...

00:18:02.624 --> 00:18:04.209
What am I doing?

00:18:04.209 --> 00:18:08.755
At this rate, I really won't
be able to be a Shepherd...

00:18:09.798 --> 00:18:11.758
I hate this.

00:18:11.758 --> 00:18:16.930
I'm going to become a Shepherd
and leave this foolish world behind!

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:30.903
Kakei, there's one more
reason why I chose you.

00:18:30.903 --> 00:18:33.989
It was written in your book.

00:18:33.989 --> 00:18:37.951
Is that a certain future?

00:18:37.951 --> 00:18:39.244
No.

00:18:39.244 --> 00:18:42.956
It's one of an infinite number of futures.

00:18:44.082 --> 00:18:47.419
It's not like I have an interest
in other people's happiness.

00:18:47.419 --> 00:18:51.507
But, is this the road I must take after all?

00:18:54.843 --> 00:18:57.763
That loneliness and despair...

00:18:57.763 --> 00:19:01.058
Maybe they were so
I could become a Shepherd.

00:19:02.226 --> 00:19:05.020
Oh, Kakei. Welcome back.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.064
Shirasaki, you're still here?

00:19:07.064 --> 00:19:09.650
I was cleaning up. Do you want tea?

00:19:10.275 --> 00:19:12.653
Sure, thanks.

00:19:13.779 --> 00:19:16.949
Um... You don't need to be with Kodachi?

00:19:16.949 --> 00:19:20.536
Oh, it wasn't anything important.

00:19:20.536 --> 00:19:22.663
I see.

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:25.624
Were you waiting for me?

00:19:25.624 --> 00:19:31.505
Huh? N-No, I wasn't waiting for you at all!

00:19:31.505 --> 00:19:33.924
Thanks, Shirasaki.

00:19:33.924 --> 00:19:37.678
I-I said, I wasn't waiting.

00:19:40.305 --> 00:19:42.766
Huh? What are these cookies for?

00:19:43.725 --> 00:19:49.565
"Miracle Lovey-Dovey Cookies"
Oh, those? U-Um, those heart ones...

00:19:49.565 --> 00:19:53.235
If two people close their eyes
and eat them at the same time...

00:19:54.194 --> 00:19:56.196
Oh, this is good!

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:04.913
Shirasaki...?

00:20:06.665 --> 00:20:08.375
Good news!

00:20:09.626 --> 00:20:11.587
What? What's going on?

00:20:11.587 --> 00:20:13.964
It's nothing...

00:20:13.964 --> 00:20:18.969
The general library is giving you
guys permission to do your activities!

00:20:21.889 --> 00:20:23.640
Really?

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:28.103
I talked with the head library
worker at the meeting this afternoon.

00:20:28.103 --> 00:20:33.775
She allowed it after I put in a good word
for you and because of your recent hard work.

00:20:33.775 --> 00:20:34.943
Oh, good!

00:20:34.943 --> 00:20:37.821
Our paradise has been protected.

00:20:38.405 --> 00:20:41.533
Thank you, Kodachi! Thank you!

00:20:41.533 --> 00:20:43.452
Kodachi, seriously, thanks.

00:20:43.452 --> 00:20:45.787
I've returned the favor from yesterday.

00:20:45.787 --> 00:20:48.040
I won't lose from now on...

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:52.002
I'm the only one that
needs to become a Shepherd!

00:20:52.002 --> 00:20:56.298
Well, I haven't really decided
what I want to do yet...

00:20:57.341 --> 00:20:58.217
"Student Council Room"

00:20:58.217 --> 00:21:00.677
This is the report from
the Library Workers Committee.

00:21:00.677 --> 00:21:04.973
They officially recognize the
Happy Project activities of the Library Club

00:21:04.973 --> 00:21:07.059
and allow them inside the general library.

00:21:07.059 --> 00:21:12.940
I see. I suppose that means they have
finally found a public place to belong.

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:16.109
He started this after
turning down my invitation...

00:21:16.109 --> 00:21:18.237
He'd better work hard at it.

00:21:18.987 --> 00:21:22.074
President, please be careful.

00:21:22.074 --> 00:21:26.620
If that face gets on the web news,
it will turn into a scandal.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:28.705
Th-That's not it, Takigawa.

00:21:28.705 --> 00:21:32.334
I was merely assessing the
activities of Kakei and the others--

00:21:32.334 --> 00:21:35.629
The Library Club cannot be crushed just yet.

00:21:35.629 --> 00:21:37.089
Huh?

00:21:50.936 --> 00:21:59.695
<i>The starting bell, the sound of a lock</i>

00:21:59.695 --> 00:22:07.369
<i>While drifting aimlessly, I become an adult</i>

00:22:07.369 --> 00:22:17.212
<i>The time has come when days spent</i>
<i>running and playing seem far away</i>

00:22:17.212 --> 00:22:21.466
<i>The answer I gave here</i>

00:22:21.466 --> 00:22:34.396
<i>Oh, if only it had been</i>
<i>passed down somewhere</i>

00:22:34.396 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>For those crowds walking around lost</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:43.530
<i>It can be a light that shines on them</i>

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:51.830
<i>On the other side of the</i>
<i>green belt that surrounds us</i>

00:22:51.830 --> 00:23:00.214
<i>You head toward endless tomorrows</i>

00:23:12.893 --> 00:23:14.811
Kakei, what are you reading?

00:23:14.811 --> 00:23:16.563
An anthology of famous sayings by wise men.

00:23:16.563 --> 00:23:17.773
Oh, speaking of famous sayings,

00:23:17.773 --> 00:23:21.068
there's this thing that's popular among
the girls working at Appllio right now.

00:23:21.068 --> 00:23:21.735
Huh?

00:23:21.735 --> 00:23:24.446
When we put in an order to
the kitchen, at the end, we say:

00:23:24.446 --> 00:23:27.533
"I'm gonna take a shot at your heart!"

00:23:27.533 --> 00:23:28.534
O-Oh...

00:23:28.534 --> 00:23:30.619
And then the response from the kitchen is...

00:23:30.619 --> 00:23:31.203
Swoon...

00:23:31.203 --> 00:23:33.497
"Next time: The Library Club's Day Off"
Yeah, yeah! Wait, how do you know?

00:23:33.497 --> 00:23:37.835
"Next time: The Library Club's Day Off"
I-I want to die...
